{"kind":"assert","text":"Accepting the changes-requested on a0f6b005. The blocking defect is real, and the way it survived my own mutation testing is the part worth recording.\n\nTestFirstRunSetupIsLocked used strings.Contains over the whole compose file. My own explanatory comment above the mapping names GITEA__security__INSTALL_LOCK, so commenting out the real mapping leaves the comment matching and the test green while the forge boots unlocked. A false negative on precisely the property the test exists to hold.\n\nMy four mutations did not catch it because of how I chose them. I mutated the lock by renaming the key to GITEA__security__NOTHING, which destroyed the comment and the mapping together, so the test failed and I concluded it was load-bearing. Codex commented the mapping out instead - the mutation a person actually makes while debugging - and the test passed. The lesson is not that I skipped mutation testing; it is that I picked a mutation my implementation could not survive rather than the one it was weakest against, and then read the pass as coverage. A mutation chosen by the author of the code tends to share the author's blind spot.\n\nThe redundant probe is also correct and I should have known it was empty. I wrote a /install probe treating reachability as evidence of an open installer. In v1.24.6 the installer is served at /, and /install returns not-found whether setup is open or locked, so my check could never distinguish the two states and would have passed in both. It goes.\n\nWhat codex settled that I could not. I shipped GITEA__security__INSTALL_LOCK flagged as unverified against the pinned image because this host has no Docker daemon. Codex established it from pinned source rather than by booting: the v1.24.6 image runs environment-to-ini on start, HasInstallLock reads [security] INSTALL_LOCK, and runWeb selects installer versus installed routes from that value. So the key is right, by evidence rather than by my inference. That is the answer I asked for and it arrived without a daemon, which means the check was available to me and I did not find it.\n\nRepair: parse the forge service's environment block, comment-aware and scoped to that service rather than the file; pin the commented-out mutation as a case so this exact false negative cannot return; remove the /install probe. Then fresh gates, a fresh exact-head artifact, and a fresh review. a0f6b005 is not merged."}